[[:db/retract 17592186104542 :answer-field/choices 17592186104544] [:db/retract 17592186104542 :answer-field/choices 17592186104545] [:db/retract 17592186104542 :answer-field/choices 17592186104546] [:db/retract 17592186104542 :answer-field/choices 17592186104547] [:db/retract 17592186104542 :answer-field/choices 17592186104543] {:db/id 17592186105926 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-718c9427-3023-5517-97ab-03ae81fa561f" "question-091cd0a0-5fb3-5e37-b062-d7bbb3f0f6e3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105521 :question/problem "Suppose that a line segment has a length of $2\\,\\textrm{m},$ and that $A$ and $B$ are its endpoints. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\overline{AB} = 2\\,\\textrm{m}$\n\nII. $\\overline{BA} = 2\\,\\textrm{m}$\n\nIII. $AB = 2\\,\\textrm{m}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The notation $\\overline{AB}$ represents the line segment itself, not the length of the line segment. Therefore, the expression ${\\overline{AB}}=2\\,\\textrm{m}$ is not valid. Instead, it should say $AB = 2 \\, \\textrm{m}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\overline{BA}$ represents the line segment itself, not the length of the line segment. Therefore, the expression ${\\overline{BA}}=2\\,\\textrm{m}$ is not valid.\n\n- Statement III is true. The notation $AB$ represents the length of the line segment $\\overline{AB},$ and this line segments has a length of $2\\,\\textrm{m}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB = 2\\,\\textrm{m}\n$$\n\nis a correct statement.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105927 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b6e9a199-9ae7-5749-8e50-9bec321630b9" "question-2b5924f6-1b4f-5cd0-89f3-79b22bdc59d5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105522 :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of a side of one cell is \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{10\\,\\textrm{mm}}{2} = 5\\,\\textrm{mm}.\n$$\n\nThe line segment has a length of $7$ cells, so the total measure is \n\n$$\nML = 7 \\cdot 5\\,\\textrm{mm} = 35\\,\\textrm{mm}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105928 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-13ca1ca9-18d5-5bc5-a895-698275236baa" "question-f3042f6b-9d86-5ac2-aea7-7fc852598853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105523 :question/problem "The ruler shown below allows measuring length both in $\\textrm{cm}$ (centimeters) and $\\textrm{in}$ (inches). Determine the measure of the line segment $\\overline{MN}.$\n\n![](images/e1/e1d80c4344e4051f1b58a8c7ec1db9930f06d679c1a0532e83bfc7bdb719c4c1.png)" :question/worked-solution "Note that $M$ is not aligned with the zero-mark on the ruler. \n\nTo find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $M$ and $N,$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the picture, we see that $M$ corresponds to $0.5\\,\\textrm{in}$ while $N$ corresponds to $2\\,\\textrm{in}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN=2\\,\\text{in}-0.5\\,\\text{in}=1.5\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105929 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-41aa9532-ccbf-54f2-a095-f66029205574" "question-751ce1db-dc08-51e0-8ae8-024841607cc5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105524 :question/worked-solution "To find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that $A$ corresponds to $10$ units while $B$ corresponds to $50$ units.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nAB = 50 - 10 = 40\\,\\textrm{units}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-718c9427-3023-5517-97ab-03ae81fa561f" :question/id #uuid "718c9427-3023-5517-97ab-03ae81fa561f" :question/math-academy-id "q-20579" :question/problem "![](images/ba/ba75204629bffa2aea805fa09cd3b5bd01c24f28edd7ba7d154b93fa9b16e5a0.png)\n\nFor the figure shown above, how many line segments are there?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we can count $6$ line segments:\n$\\overset{―}{PQ}$ , $\\overset{―}{PR}$, $\\overset{―}{PS}$ , $\\overset{―}{QR}$ , $\\overset{―}{QS}$, $\\overset{―}{RS}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ec988d28-c733-5206-8eca-d45a06bdcdd9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ec988d28-c733-5206-8eca-d45a06bdcdd9" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec988d28-c733-5206-8eca-d45a06bdcdd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b19b68f1-5299-5a47-9d9a-713b9cee64c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2e959fa5-8b29-5607-9d43-2eadc057ddb4" "answer-e312ad0f-01d3-5aba-880c-ee952aa7d0e4" "answer-41dae19a-3d1e-5205-b6d7-7d5ead048a21" "answer-40e95413-e09d-56c8-8429-95b89c3e104b" "answer-b19b68f1-5299-5a47-9d9a-713b9cee64c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e959fa5-8b29-5607-9d43-2eadc057ddb4" :answer/id #uuid "2e959fa5-8b29-5607-9d43-2eadc057ddb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e312ad0f-01d3-5aba-880c-ee952aa7d0e4" :answer/id #uuid "e312ad0f-01d3-5aba-880c-ee952aa7d0e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41dae19a-3d1e-5205-b6d7-7d5ead048a21" :answer/id #uuid "41dae19a-3d1e-5205-b6d7-7d5ead048a21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40e95413-e09d-56c8-8429-95b89c3e104b" :answer/id #uuid "40e95413-e09d-56c8-8429-95b89c3e104b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b19b68f1-5299-5a47-9d9a-713b9cee64c4" :answer/id #uuid "b19b68f1-5299-5a47-9d9a-713b9cee64c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-091cd0a0-5fb3-5e37-b062-d7bbb3f0f6e3" :question/id #uuid "091cd0a0-5fb3-5e37-b062-d7bbb3f0f6e3" :question/math-acade